{"kind":"request","text":"ARC-1 concrete design questions under ruling80026b71, from note4a511674 and resultb4fca32a. Please rule on two choices before production.\n\n1. May ARC-1 introduce bounded provider staging and paged archive publication/reader assembly, and who owns that contract after AE-1? The current provider binds credentials only to journalRef(scope), final append verifies supplied objects, finish/manifest sources cap at64 and one transfer caps at8MiB.128 maximum copies alone are32MiB. Preparing maps of64 does not solve final publication. Proposed contract binds each stage to repository/scope/entry-hash/ordinal; all local+foreign metadata classification completes before any payload upload; provider read-back precedes cursor advancement; final complete-proof read-back alone advances the receipt. Staged admitted bytes have ordinary repository-reader visibility, including public visibility in a public repository, with no secrecy from obscure refs/IDs. Abandonment releases the staging reference but provider retention may keep bytes. Does that visibility/retention contract fit the intended provider, or must its owner supply reviewed private staging? The design will not reinterpret existing whole-manifest limits as page limits without your decision.\n\n2. Does the universal admitted-entry guarantee wait for RB-1's row/item ceilings, or should ARC-1 define an exact supported cohort and build bounded streaming for larger retained rows? Accepted bb6cf92b establishes no constant rule-row size from kernel bounds; archive-retained currently has a1MiB serving bound. No formula over usesPerEntry/entryBytes alone bounds every retained payload. The note gives the conditional finite-pass formula and rank but explicitly leaves K and complete stage-cost constants unproved.64-effect privacy versus derivedEffects256 also needs a staged owner walk for the universal claim.\n\nThe seven-point note and Security conclusion are at notes/implementation/2026-11-14-arc1-staged-archive-design.md on clean pushed head4a511674ebd8419befa9f49f6854546e2e1abaff. All other files equal main372a52f9. No source, cap/kernel change or executable validation occurred. ARC-1 stops before further design commitment or code pending these decisions and AE-1.","body":{"conditions":"Decide the staged provider/paged archive contract and the unbounded retained-row boundary before ARC-1 fills its static proof or changes production. No kernel or cap change follows; build still waits AE-1.","no_git_artifact":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bb6cf92bc08375c4405d93057d2e3639494ad2df stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b5750e6e82650d29470d64f83b0dc3a50115b466","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}